From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:40:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: apple,tristar-charger: Add the
 iPad 5 (J71t)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The iPad 5 charges through the same hardware as the iPad 6: a D2365 charger
at 0x180 with the input limit at 0xa03, and a Tristar CBTL1610 on i2c0 at
0x1a. Its PMU event line is AP GPIO 76. Add its board compatible so it uses
the shared charger.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux f5ce1082 (J71t ledger 6.1); the separate apple_j71t_charger becomes a board compatible of the shared Tristar charger]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml   | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
index 5e59cf90d..e3507f5cb 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
@@ -11,10 +11,11 @@ maintainers:
 
 description: |
   Charging on Apple devices whose Lightning port uses a Tristar (NXP CBTL1610)
-  port controller and a D2365-family PMIC. The node is a child of the PMIC.
-  It identifies the attached source through the Tristar and the PMIC ADC and
-  sets the PMIC input-current limit, which iBoot leaves at 100 mA. PMU events
-  come from the PMIC's event interrupt controller (the PMIC GPIO node).
+  port controller and a D2365-family PMIC, such as the iPad 5 and iPad 6. The
+  node is a child of the PMIC. It identifies the attached source through the
+  Tristar and the PMIC ADC and sets the PMIC input-current limit, which iBoot
+  leaves at 100 mA. PMU events come from the PMIC's event interrupt
+  controller (the PMIC GPIO node).
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: power-supply.yaml#
@@ -24,6 +25,7 @@ properties:
     items:
       - enum:
           - apple,j71b-tristar-charger
+          - apple,j71t-tristar-charger
       - const: apple,tristar-charger
 
   reg:
